            "type": "text",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "shiro-wat"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "Shiro Wat"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is made by stirring ground chickpea flour into a spiced, buttery onion base. The result is a thick, smooth stew that pours like a rich gravy. It is one of the fastest dishes in the Ethiopian repertoire and one of the most satisfying."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "If you cannot find pre-ground chickpea flour, blitz tinned chickpeas in a food processor until they become a rough powder, then sieve out any large lumps."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
